# LiveStage service settings. The root filesystem is read-only: the console's
# setup (tty1) saves the web UI's address in /var/lib/livestage/setup.conf,
# and hand-made changes go in /var/lib/livestage/livestage.conf (same
# variables), which wins over both.

# The session (mix), on the data partition.
#LIVESTAGE_SESSION="/data/livestage/show.json"
# Where takes are recorded. Unset, the storage chosen in the setup or the web
# UI (Setup → Storage): a USB drive's "LiveStage Recordings" folder, or
# /data/livestage/recordings. Set, this folder always, whatever is chosen.
#LIVESTAGE_RECORDINGS="/data/livestage/recordings"

# The web UI's address. 0.0.0.0 is every network interface; 127.0.0.1 keeps
# it to this machine. On the network, until a web user exists, a browser
# needs the setup code shown on tty1 to get in: create an admin user (Setup
# → Users) first thing, then everyone logs in with a name and PIN.
#LIVESTAGE_HTTP="0.0.0.0:8730"

# A browser must reach the web UI by an IP address, NAME.local or this
# machine's name; any other name is refused (that stops a website from
# pointing its own name here). Add other names, one --web-host each, to
# LIVESTAGE_ARGS, for example:
#   --web-host mixer.example.org

# More livestage-server arguments, for example:
#   --output "hw:CARD=USB" --input "hw:CARD=USB" --rate 48000 --buffer 128
#LIVESTAGE_ARGS=""
